                    "compulsory": true
                },
                {
                    "no": 7,
                    "code": "Caribbean & Mexico - Seaweed",
                    "description": "Caribbean & Mexico - Seaweed",
                    "note": "Seaweed - Some hotels in the Caribbean and Mexico can be affected by an \nincreased level of seaweed, known as Sargassum. This is a natural occurrence, \nwith the situation changing on a daily basis being influenced by weather patterns\n and sea currents, which we have no control over. Where affected, \nhotels will take steps to address this and work to remove the seaweed and\n minimise disturbance. For safety reasons, from time to time the water \nsports/water based activities may not be available in Mexico and the \nCaribbean due to the Sargassum, as it presents a risk of getting tangled up in \nboat engines and other equipment. Our in-resort teams are aware and\n carefully monitor the situation, as do our partners. The issue remains \nvery rare, and it is not possible to predict exactly when or where it might \nhappen",
                    "dateModified": "2025-03-12T13:20:49",
                    "external": true,
                    "internal": true,
                    "priority": "H",
                    "itemInfo": [
                        "HTL 2"
                    ],
